WEBVTT

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.310
Can this thing move?

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:16.700
Of course.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.810
I've never seen a tank like this before.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.460
It's a prototype model.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.120
My real father and my foster father wanted to make

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.750
a tank that was better than any other in existence.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:26.940
Your real father?

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:29.450
He was a Darcsen.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.170
This tank is named Edelweiss.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:35.670
Edelweiss...

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:38.270
"Noble white".

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:43.500
Can you drive it?

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.310
I practised during military training in high school.

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:47.760
What about the tank shells?

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:49.170
They're already loaded.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:50.560
What about fuel?

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:53.540
It has about a half-a-day's worth of Ragnoline.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:54.780
Good!

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:59.100
Are you sure you two just met?

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.970
Come, get on.

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:10.770
Isara, burst through!

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:11.580
Roger!

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:13.540
Welkin, beat them up!

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:18.840
Since we're going to open fire on them, "blow them up" might be more appropriate.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:21.040
Like I said, just beat them up!

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:22.680
R-Roger.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.360
Gunners, fire!

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:45.820
Drive through them!

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:53.510
Fire, fire!

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:55.220
We'll hit our own side!

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:56.090
I don't care!

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:13.090
What incredible speed...

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:18.170
Chapter 2:

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:18.170
Prayers Falling Like Snow

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:21.850
A tank! A tank's coming!

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:25.110
What? All right, I'll put a hole in it!

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:26.560
Huh?

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.420
Don't shoot!

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:33.010
Alicia's riding on that tank!

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:34.380
What did you say?

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:47.020
Alicia!

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:59.080
Isn't she a Darcsen?

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.820
Only the town watch is left in Bruhl?

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:09.290
Old man Luuben complained about leaving, but we had someone take him away by force.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:10.660
Thank goodness.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:12.750
Alicia!

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:14.800
Who are those two over there?

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:16.390
Yes, sir.

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:19.800
Let me introduce him. This is Mr. Welkin Gunther.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:22.500
He's the son of that General Gunther.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:26.710
And over here is Miss Isara Gunther.

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:29.460
She's General Gunther's adopted daughter.

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:38.440
Mr. Welkin, are you attending the University of Randgriz?

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:43.410
Yes, I am. My major is biology.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.510
Oh, you two know each other?

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:48.860
I probably met him a very long time ago.

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:52.940
My father's... in a party held by the
Evans family or something like that.

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:56.780
Susie was the one who first reported the presence of a spy.

00:03:58.290 --> 00:03:59.910
I'm really sorry!

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:02.470
I've done a very disrespectful thing!

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.970
Alicia, what's going on?

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:06.180
Give me a proper explanation.

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:08.700
Yes.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:10.920
The Imperial Army destroyed the Gunthers' house.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:14.150
I believe they're advancing their troops to the heart of Bruhl.

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:16.360
Advancing their troops?!

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:19.310
Wait a minute, Alicia.

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:21.970
Don't tell me you ran away from there?

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:23.010
Yes.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:26.320
You mean to say that you led them all the way here?

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:29.140
Some town watch member you are!

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:31.870
We can buy some time if we lure them here, right?

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:36.140
The Imperial Army is in a state of disorder right now.

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:39.030
They got attacked by some tank they've never seen before,

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:40.960
and on top of that, they let us slip away.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:44.060
They'll definitely come after us.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:45.930
To uphold the name of the Imperial Army.

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:53.230
Then the town watch will only need to hold out until all the townspeople have been evacuated to the Military's side.

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:56.100
I don't think there can be a better solution.

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:58.380
H-Hold out, you say?

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:01.330
When the crossfire starts, even the Gallian Army will have to take action.

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:02.650
Do you think everything will go that smoothly?

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:04.060
I do think so.

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:12.810
As Chief Laaken's deputy, I will take command from here.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:14.250
There is no objection, is there?

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:28.390
We have these when the situation calls for it.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:31.470
With a little maintenence, they should become usable in actual combat.

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:35.990
That thing's so old it wouldn't even splutter.

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:36.690
Yeah...

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:39.780
Umm, I have a question.

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:41.550
What is it, son?

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:44.670
When do we run away?

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:45.650
Welkin!

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:48.980
You want us to run away like cowards?

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:53.870
I don't know about the coward part, but I think we have no choice but to retreat.

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:58.410
Son, do you have experience in the frontline?

00:05:58.410 --> 00:05:59.450
I haven't.

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:01.470
Is that so?

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:05.130
I was in the Militia during the First War.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:08.700
Huh? No, that's not what I was asking.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:10.050
I was asking about the timing of the retreat.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:15.320
That's for me to decide.

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:19.560
Just keep still so that you don't fall down and sprain your ankle.

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:24.400
Welkin and Isara can operate the Edelweiss!

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:28.250
Do you mean to let these cowards with no
experience on the front lines join us in battle?

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:30.450
He'll just shoot us in the back at best.

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:33.340
I'll go feed the Imperial Army some bullets.

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:36.490
In the meantime, prepare the tanks for deployment.

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:37.530
Let's go!

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:45.740
Seriously, don't say something so pathetic at this kind of time!

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:46.630
I can't believe you!

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:48.770
Pathetic?

00:06:48.770 --> 00:06:49.730
What's pathetic?

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:52.190
You only think about saving your own skin!

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:54.220
You still call yourself the General's son?

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:57.680
Well, genetically speaking, I am his son.

00:06:58.030 --> 00:07:00.140
But I need to take care of myself too.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.420
Forget it!

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:05.840
I see them! The Imperial Army!

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:08.280
There's... one, two, three tanks...

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:10.350
They have six tanks!

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:11.730
It's a regimental assault!

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.420
One hour.

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:20.160
I don't want my feet in the mud of this nasty rural town any longer than that.

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:22.120
All troops, charge!

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:26.580
We have to contact Mr. Laaken!

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:36.170
Fire, fire!

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:37.470
Everyone, take them all down!

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:48.610
Damn! If only we were as well equipped as the Military...

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:49.940
Then this wouldn't be happening!

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:05.580
The Sister Mills...

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.160
The west gate! Head for the west gate!

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:09.050
Do a flank assault!

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:11.720
I can't! The Imperial Army is already there!

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:12.840
What?!

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:15.800
Bloody hell! I'll show you the spirit of a Gallian!

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:16.420
Stop!

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:33.600
Damn... If only we had a tank...

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:44.710
How's the tank's maintenence going?

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:46.620
It's still not in working condition...

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:47.450
Hurry up!

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:51.260
I've done a check, but the engine plug...

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:55.090
I don't think a Darcsen is fit to teach me anything.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:58.760
Good!

00:08:58.760 --> 00:08:59.720
Wait, please!

00:09:00.380 --> 00:09:03.270
This tank's still undergoing maintenence!

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:04.180
If you move out like that...

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:05.300
Go!

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:14.110
Hello? Hello?

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:19.810
I'm fed up with this broken-down radio!

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:23.140
There are times when you get signal after hitting it,

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:26.230
but I don't think you need to hit that hard.

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:28.770
Actually, I was just venting my anger on it.

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:33.090
Is this the only way of getting in contact with the chief of the town watch?

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:36.860
Alternatively, I can go talk to him in person.

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:41.410
But I've got no idea whether he's in Landbaste or on his way there.

00:09:41.410 --> 00:09:44.590
Now that's a cause for concern.

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:48.410
Welkin, please stop him!

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:51.650
That tank mustn't move out!

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:00.820
Just you wait, Imperials!

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:07.580
All right, I'll blow you away!

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:14.120
See? I destroyed an Imperial tank!

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:16.000
By the hands of this Melken Suustein!

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:17.670
Push forward!

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:18.550
Charge!

00:10:29.890 --> 00:10:30.770
What's wrong?

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:32.730
Well, it suddenly...

00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:34.440
Damn it!

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:40.360
There he is!

00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:43.570
Wait! Something doesn't look right.

00:10:44.250 --> 00:10:46.160
It's hopeless! It can't move!

00:10:49.910 --> 00:10:52.260
Damn, the enemy tank is here!

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:54.250
Never mind it! Run!

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:10.330
Alicia, we've run out of bandages and medicine!

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:12.090
What should we do?

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:17.330
There are probably seven to ten dead town watch members.

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:19.400
And more than twenty who are injured.

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:20.940
We're out of luck!

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:23.860
There are Imperial soldiers at both the west gate and the north street!

00:11:23.860 --> 00:11:25.740
Jan and I went to check on them!

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:28.230
Give us a bit more time and...

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:35.290
If I could fly, I could drop grenades on the Imperial soldiers' heads!

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:41.290
Chief!

00:11:43.270 --> 00:11:44.630
Mr. Laaken!

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:47.340
You have done well.

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:48.930
The evacuation is complete.

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:50.800
The townspeople are all safe and sound.

00:11:54.050 --> 00:11:54.900
What about the Military?

00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:58.250
The order to dispatch has already been issued.

00:11:58.250 --> 00:12:01.170
They're heading here at full speed.

00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:05.910
It seems we're a bit late.

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:09.370
But the town watch has done its duty well.

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:12.530
Which means... what's left for us is to run away.

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:15.120
What's left? You speak of it so lightly, Welkin!

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:16.580
I'm not correct?

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:22.040
Honestly... you say that like it's something easy to do.

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:28.060
Reporting in!

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:30.720
We have gained control of everything, including the west gate.

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:32.140
Good work.

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:32.600
Yes, sir!

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:35.640
What's left is the enemy headquarters, huh?

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:40.690
But where is that odd tank?

00:12:41.300 --> 00:12:44.980
But why? Didn't you plan to be the first to run away?

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:47.430
I'd like to, if I could.

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:53.970
But the best method of retreat is for the Edelweiss to move out.

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:57.670
Isara, are you not afraid too?

00:12:57.670 --> 00:13:01.050
The Edelweiss is our father's keepsake.

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:03.130
I don't want anyone else to touch it.

00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:11.320
Mr. Laaken! We can only stall the enemy for about thirty minutes.

00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:12.550
Good enough!

00:13:12.550 --> 00:13:14.510
Sorry, but I'm counting on you!

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:16.220
Yes, sir!

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:20.560
From here, we'll attack the enemy base.

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:23.280
All troops, advance!

00:13:33.090 --> 00:13:34.420
You finally came.

00:13:34.420 --> 00:13:35.200
Fire!

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:43.560
My army has greater firepower!

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:44.710
Aim for its tracks!

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:48.140
They're coming!

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:55.590
Isara!

00:13:55.590 --> 00:13:56.890
Turning!

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:01.940
Shoot that thing!

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:03.730
R-Roger!

00:14:12.110 --> 00:14:14.100
Susie, hurry up!

00:14:14.100 --> 00:14:15.630
Yes!

00:14:24.940 --> 00:14:26.760
What a monster...

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:27.860
Sir!

00:14:28.870 --> 00:14:30.640
The Gallian Army is approaching!

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:31.590
What?

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:35.430
Pull out for now! Pull out!

00:14:39.340 --> 00:14:42.320
The Imperial Army is retreating...

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:03.340
Let's go. Everyone must be worried about us.

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:06.180
Is it all right not to go after the Imperial Army?

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:07.480
Why?

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:09.290
I thought you'd certainly do that.

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:14.270
We'll only increase the casualty count if we chase them too far.

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:17.480
Right now, as long as everyone gets out safely...

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:31.230
Do you plan to abandon Bruhl like this?

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:43.490
Alicia!

00:15:56.920 --> 00:16:02.560
Before all this, I was working at a bakery, and life in the town was tranquil...

00:16:04.120 --> 00:16:09.440
I never thought I'd see Bruhl like this... Even now, I can't believe it...

00:16:28.470 --> 00:16:30.420
That's a lion's paw, isn't it?{daffodils, ya ignant elevens >_<}

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:33.300
Yes!

00:16:33.820 --> 00:16:37.610
It'd be nice if the field were covered with flowers.

00:16:37.610 --> 00:16:42.530
But... it's only going to get worse from now on, isn't it?

00:16:42.530 --> 00:16:46.860
It looks like the Military has decided to abandon Bruhl.

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:51.100
Even so... Even so, I'm sure that the flowers will bloom someday,

00:16:51.100 --> 00:16:51.850
Susie.

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:08.960
The circle of life turns and the world continues to change.

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:12.000
Even though the lion's paw looks like it's all dried up,

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:15.420
it will go to seed and bud again one day.{yes, this /is/ correct gardening terminology}

00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:17.550
The same goes for the fish and the birds.

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:22.720
In order to keep living, no animal can avoid conflict.

00:17:22.720 --> 00:17:24.050
Humans can't, either.

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:29.370
But this world isn't built merely upon strife.

00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:33.810
There has to be a way to co-exist and thrive together.

00:17:34.370 --> 00:17:35.520
Together...

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:40.150
I've been thinking that maybe I can search for that way.

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:47.120
I think I'll join the Militia.

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:52.500
But why? We just barely managed to escape alive!

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:56.230
I've decided to do what I can.

00:17:56.230 --> 00:17:59.170
So... that means fighting?

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:04.360
To end the fighting.

00:18:04.360 --> 00:18:07.080
And I'll definitely come back.

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:09.470
Back to this Bruhl where the lion's paws bloom.

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:18.650
To everyone in the town watch, I will never let your deaths be in vain.

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:02.160
Hey, Alicia?

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:05.060
Is my ribbon okay?

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:06.350
It doesn't look odd, does it?

00:19:06.350 --> 00:19:07.370
Not at all.

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:09.020
That uniform looks nice on you.

00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:15.260
My father was delighted when he heard I was joining the Militia!

00:19:15.260 --> 00:19:18.040
"I'd expect nothing less from an Evans", he said.

00:19:19.460 --> 00:19:21.970
Is Sergeant Alicia Melchiott here?

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:24.220
Yes, that's me.

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:28.260
The commander of the 3rd Regiment has given orders that you come immediately...

00:19:28.260 --> 00:19:30.100
...to give a report on the situation during Bruhl's retreat.

00:19:32.380 --> 00:19:34.190
Why me?

00:19:47.220 --> 00:19:49.100
Sergeant Alicia Melchiott!

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:51.150
Yes!

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:56.040
Ouch!

00:19:56.460 --> 00:19:57.870
I'm sorry.

00:19:57.870 --> 00:20:00.780
Because I was thinking about something...

00:20:04.360 --> 00:20:05.970
Huh? Alicia?

00:20:07.220 --> 00:20:08.820
Welkin!

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:13.980
The lion's paw is a perennial plant that grows wild in open fields.

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:16.690
It's said to be effective for relieving pain and alleviating fever.

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:18.220
Oh, excuse me.

00:20:18.220 --> 00:20:20.100
I'm Welkin Gunther.

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:21.620
My hobby is observing nature.

00:20:21.620 --> 00:20:24.380
I'm studying biology at university, too.

00:20:24.380 --> 00:20:29.500
It seems I have to take leave from school for a while, but I'll make up for it at the Amatriain Base.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:33.500
Next time on Valkyria Chronicles, Chapter 3.

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:34.930
Birth of the 7th Platoon.

00:20:34.930 --> 00:20:40.000
Chapter 3:

